Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:43:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 080/154] feat(devbar): the bubble reads, hides on a scroll
 down, and returns on a scroll up
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE BUBBLE is 0.94 alpha now, up from 0.82, which read as fog over a
busy page.

IT SLIDES AWAY on a downward scroll and comes back on an upward one,
the way Safari's compact field does. The pinch monitor, a local NSEvent
monitor the window already runs, hands plain wheel deltas to the
window: the widget host's input observer saw the keys and never a
wheel. DevBarScrollAway turns the deltas into a state with a 12px dead
zone and a count that starts over on every turn. A navigation or a
toggle brings the bar back.

THE CORNERS: the widget's own background is cleared when the devbar
page reports ready. At creation the render view did not exist yet, so
the clear at that point did nothing, and a square of widget background
showed at the corners on a white page.

THE PAGE TINT SETTING, turned off, clears the band. Since a tint no
longer floods the backdrop, restoring the space tint alone left the
glow up.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
